IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Alabama Family Assistance (TANF cash assistance): Code of Alabama 1975, Title 38, Chapters 1, 4 and 11A, with the
-- Department of Human Resources' grant rules in the Alabama Administrative Code, chapter 660-2-2.
--
-- Edition:
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ala-code-38-1.txt, ala-code-38-4.txt, ala-code-38-11a.txt -- the Code as ALISON served
--   it on 2026-10-20 (no 'current through' date published);
--   ../../../alabama-administrative-code-660-2-2-and-660-2-4-family-assistance-payment-and-state-supplementation/
--   registers/source-bundle/ala-admin-code-660-2-2-and-660-2-4.txt -- rules 660-2-2-.10, -.27, -.31, -.32 as the
--   Administrative Code showed them on 2026-10-19.
--
-- In: s 38-4-1(a), (d) (aid to dependent children: who it is payable for); s 38-4-2(a) (written notice of the action
-- taken); s 38-4-4(a) (the duty to report new income or resources), (b) (federal Title IV-A standards govern; the 60-month
-- limit of 42 U.S.C. 608(a)(7) is asked as a fact); s 38-4-5 (appeal for a fair hearing); s 38-11A-2(b), (c) (three job
-- applications; quitting or refusing work); s 38-1-8 (drug felony offenders); r 660-2-2-.10, -.27, -.31, -.32 (need test,
-- grant, $10 minimum, first-month proration).
--
-- Not in the deposited text, so INPUTS: the payment standard for the family's size (r 660-2-2-.31 says the Department set
-- one; the attachment that held it was repealed in 2018, and no current table is deposited: ADMIN-POLICY), and the family's
-- rounded total net countable income (the income disregards are DHR policy, not deposited).
--
-- Out: old age pensions, aid to the blind and to the permanently and totally disabled (s 38-4-1(b), (c), (e)); the State
-- Supplementation rules (660-2-4); SNAP (federal: subjects/us/food-and-nutrition-act-of-2008); s 38-4-14, s 38-4-15
-- (spending limits on benefits); sanctions under rr 660-2-2-.18 and -.23 (not deposited); recoupment.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the applicant (the parent or caretaker relative applying for a needy child).
-- Expected values in the case file are hand-written. No pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT ADVICE.

§ `Alabama Family Assistance (TANF cash assistance)`

§§ `s 38-4-1(d) -- for whom aid to dependent children is payable`

DECLARE `Application` HAS
    -- s 38-4-1(d): "a dependent child as defined in the Federal Social Security Act" (42 U.S.C. 606, as it stood; now
    -- the Title IV-A rules): a borrowed term, asked as a fact
    `the child is a dependent child under the Social Security Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child makes his or her home in Alabama`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `property was disposed of to qualify`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving another federally matched public assistance`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38-4-1(a): no assistance to an inmate of a public institution (exceptions where federal matching allows)
    `the child is an inmate of a public institution`               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38-11A-2(b)
    `unsubsidized jobs applied for before completing the application` IS A NUMBER
    `complying with the required work activities`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38-11A-2(c)
    `quit or refused employment without good cause while receiving` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38-1-8
    `convicted of a drug-related felony`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed the sentence`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfactorily serving probation`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 38-4-4(b) and 42 U.S.C. 608(a)(7): months of assistance already received as an adult; a hardship exemption is
    -- the state's to grant
    `months of TANF assistance already received as an adult`       IS A NUMBER
    `granted a hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- r 660-2-2-.27, -.31: both inputs (see the header)
    `rounded total net countable income`                           IS A NUMBER
    `payment standard for the family's size`                       IS A NUMBER

§§ `rr 660-2-2-.10, -.27, -.32 -- need and the amount`

-- r 660-2-2-.32: "The grant amount is computed by subtracting rounded total net income from the payment standard."
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deficit` MEANS
    a's `payment standard for the family's size` MINUS a's `rounded total net countable income`

-- r 660-2-2-.10: "The minimum grant is $10." r 660-2-2-.27: the family "must not have total net countable income equal to
-- or in excess of the appropriate payment standard subject to the minimum payment regulations of Rule No. 660-2-2-.10".
-- Read as: the deficit must be at least $10 (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needy under the payment standard` IF
    `the deficit` a AT LEAST 10

§§ `s 38-1-8 -- drug felony offenders`

-- "a person convicted of a drug related felony who is otherwise ineligible ... shall be eligible for the aid upon
-- completion of his or her sentence or if the person is satisfactorily serving a sentence of a period of probation".
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not barred as a drug felony offender` IF
        NOT (a's `convicted of a drug-related felony`)
    OR  a's `completed the sentence`
    OR  a's `satisfactorily serving probation`

§§ `Eligibility`

-- s 38-4-1(d)(1)-(4), s 38-4-1(a), s 38-11A-2(b), (c), s 38-1-8, s 38-4-4(b) with 42 U.S.C. 608(a)(7), r 660-2-2-.27.
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for Family Assistance` IF
        a's `the child is a dependent child under the Social Security Act`
    AND `needy under the payment standard` a
    AND a's `the child makes his or her home in Alabama`
    AND (NOT (a's `property was disposed of to qualify`))
    AND (NOT (a's `receiving another federally matched public assistance`))
    AND (NOT (a's `the child is an inmate of a public institution`))
    AND a's `unsubsidized jobs applied for before completing the application` AT LEAST 3
    AND a's `complying with the required work activities`
    AND (NOT (a's `quit or refused employment without good cause while receiving`))
    AND `not barred as a drug felony offender` a
    AND (a's `months of TANF assistance already received as an adult` LESS THAN 60 OR a's `granted a hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`)

-- r 660-2-2-.10: the deficit "is to be the grant amount subject to the minimum payment requirement, except when the
-- initial payment is authorized for the month of the application and is prorated from the date the application was
-- received". r 660-2-2-.32: the prorated amount is the full month's amount "multiplied by the ratio of the number of days in
-- the month including and following the date of application to 30 days". So a prorated first payment is not held to the
-- $10 minimum (finding 4). No rounding of the prorated amount is stated.
GIVEN `date of application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the month from the date of application` MEANS
    `the first day of the next month` `date of application` MINUS `date of application`

GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the next month` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `d` EQUALS 12
    THEN Date 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `d` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `d`)

GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly grant` MEANS
    IF `eligible for Family Assistance` a
    THEN `the deficit` a
    ELSE 0

GIVEN a IS AN `Application`, `date of application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grant for the month of application` MEANS
    IF `eligible for Family Assistance` a
    THEN `the deficit` a TIMES (`the days in the month from the date of application` `date of application` DIVIDED BY 30)
    ELSE 0

§§ `Duties and rights`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the applicant`
    `the county director`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the county department of the new income or resources`
    `give the applicant written notice of the action taken`
    `appeal to the state department for a fair hearing`

-- s 38-4-4(a): if the recipient, spouse or cohabiting partner "shall become possessed of any income or resources in excess
-- of that owned or being received at the date of the application, it shall be the duty of the recipient immediately to
-- notify the county department". "Immediately" is taken as within one day (finding 6). The county department then must
-- "continue, reduce or cancel" the grant "as the facts may warrant", subject to appeal.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to report new income` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `notify the county department of the new income or resources`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 38-4-4(a): new income or resources not reported immediately"

-- s 38-4-2(a): "The county director shall give notice in writing to the applicant of the action taken on his application
-- or any subsequent change in payments." No time is stated (the investigation is to be "promptly made").
GIVEN `director` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to give written notice` `director` MEANS
    PARTY `director`
    MUST  `give the applicant written notice of the action taken`

-- s 38-4-5: a person denied the right to apply, whose application "is not acted upon with reasonable promptness or is
-- denied", whose assistance is not granted promptly, or who deems the amount or terms unjust, "may appeal to the state
-- department for a hearing". No time limit is in the statute (finding 7), so no WITHIN.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to a fair hearing` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MAY   `appeal to the state department for a fair hearing`

GIVEN `denied the right to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not acted upon with reasonable promptness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `denied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not granted promptly after eligibility was established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or terms deemed unjust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may appeal for a fair hearing` IF
        `denied the right to apply`
    OR  `not acted upon with reasonable promptness`
    OR  `denied`
    OR  `not granted promptly after eligibility was established`
    OR  `the amount or terms deemed unjust`

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the applicant`
-- The seat: the parent or caretaker relative who applies for Family Assistance for a needy child, and later the recipient.

§§ `Can I get Family Assistance?`

@export Is my family eligible for Alabama Family Assistance (TANF cash assistance) (Ala. Code ss 38-4-1(d), 38-11A-2, 38-1-8; Ala. Admin. Code r 660-2-2-.27)?
GIVEN `my child is a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your child a "dependent child" under the federal TANF rules (generally, a child under 18, or under 19 in secondary school, living with a parent or caretaker relative)?
      `my child lives in Alabama` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your child make his or her home in Alabama?
      `I gave away property to qualify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you or the child give away or get rid of property in order to qualify?
      `we get other federally matched assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child receiving any other public assistance that the federal government matches?
      `my child is in a public institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child an inmate of a public institution?
      `jobs I applied for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many unsubsidized jobs did you apply for before completing the application?
      `I am doing the required work activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you complying with the job search, education and other employment activities DHR requires?
      `I quit or refused work without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While receiving assistance, did you quit a job or refuse employment without good cause?
      `I have a drug felony conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of a drug-related felony?
      `I have completed my sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have you completed your sentence?
      `I am satisfactorily on probation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you satisfactorily serving a period of probation?
      `months of TANF I have had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of TANF assistance have you already received as an adult (in any state)?
      `I have a hardship exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has DHR granted you a hardship exemption from the 60-month limit?
      `our rounded net countable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your assistance group's rounded total net countable monthly income, as DHR counts it, in US dollars
      `the payment standard for my family` IS A NUMBER @desc DHR's monthly payment standard for a family of your size, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my family eligible for Family Assistance` MEANS
    `eligible for Family Assistance` (`the application from` `my child is a dependent child` `my child lives in Alabama` `I gave away property to qualify` `we get other federally matched assistance` `my child is in a public institution` `jobs I applied for` `I am doing the required work activities` `I quit or refused work without good cause` `I have a drug felony conviction` `I have completed my sentence` `I am satisfactorily on probation` `months of TANF I have had` `I have a hardship exemption` `our rounded net countable income` `the payment standard for my family`)

§§ `How much would I get?`

@export How much Alabama Family Assistance would my family get for a full month (Ala. Admin. Code rr 660-2-2-.10, -.32)? 0 means not eligible.
GIVEN `our rounded net countable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your assistance group's rounded total net countable monthly income, as DHR counts it, in US dollars
      `the payment standard for my family` IS A NUMBER @desc DHR's monthly payment standard for a family of your size, in US dollars
      `we meet the other conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet every other condition of eligibility (dependent child, Alabama home, three job applications, work activities, no disqualification, under 60 months)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- The other conditions are folded into the first argument; the remaining eligibility slots get fixed passing values.
`How much Family Assistance would we get a month` MEANS
    `the monthly grant` (`the application from` `we meet the other conditions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE `our rounded net countable income` `the payment standard for my family`)

@export How much Alabama Family Assistance would my family get for the month in which I applied (Ala. Admin. Code r 660-2-2-.32)?
GIVEN `our rounded net countable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your assistance group's rounded total net countable monthly income, as DHR counts it, in US dollars
      `the payment standard for my family` IS A NUMBER @desc DHR's monthly payment standard for a family of your size, in US dollars
      `we meet the other conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet every other condition of eligibility?
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date DHR received your application
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much would we get for the month I applied` MEANS
    `the grant for the month of application` (`the application from` `we meet the other conditions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE `our rounded net countable income` `the payment standard for my family`) `the day I applied`

§§ `If DHR turns me down or I disagree`

@export Can I appeal to the Alabama Department of Human Resources for a fair hearing about my assistance (Ala. Code s 38-4-5)?
GIVEN `I was not allowed to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you denied the right to apply?
      `my application was not acted on promptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application not acted on with reasonable promptness?
      `my application was denied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application denied?
      `payment did not start promptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was assistance not granted promptly after you were found eligible?
      `I think the amount is unjust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consider the amount or terms of your award, or a change to it, unjust?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I appeal for a fair hearing` MEANS
    `may appeal for a fair hearing` `I was not allowed to apply` `my application was not acted on promptly` `my application was denied` `payment did not start promptly` `I think the amount is unjust`

-- Builds the application record from plain inputs, in the order of the record.
GIVEN `dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN, `home in Alabama` IS A BOOLEAN, `disposed` IS A BOOLEAN, `other assistance` IS A BOOLEAN, `inmate` IS A BOOLEAN, `jobs` IS A NUMBER, `work activities` IS A BOOLEAN, `quit` IS A BOOLEAN, `felony` IS A BOOLEAN, `completed` IS A BOOLEAN, `probation` IS A BOOLEAN, `months` IS A NUMBER, `hardship` IS A BOOLEAN, `income` IS A NUMBER, `standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Application`
`the application from` MEANS
    `Application` WITH
        `the child is a dependent child under the Social Security Act`  IS `dependent child`
        `the child makes his or her home in Alabama`                   IS `home in Alabama`
        `property was disposed of to qualify`                          IS `disposed`
        `receiving another federally matched public assistance`        IS `other assistance`
        `the child is an inmate of a public institution`               IS `inmate`
        `unsubsidized jobs applied for before completing the application` IS `jobs`
        `complying with the required work activities`                  IS `work activities`
        `quit or refused employment without good cause while receiving` IS `quit`
        `convicted of a drug-related felony`                           IS `felony`
        `completed the sentence`                                       IS `completed`
        `satisfactorily serving probation`                             IS `probation`
        `months of TANF assistance already received as an adult`       IS `months`
        `granted a hardship exemption from the 60-month limit`         IS `hardship`
        `rounded total net countable income`                           IS `income`
        `payment standard for the family's size`                       IS `standard`
